# Orchestration-layer operational state — not part of the effort's record
.omc/
.DS_Store

# Linked worktrees live inside `.claude/`, and `.claude/` became a TRACKED
# directory on 2026-08-16 when the end-session overlay landed in it. Without
# this line a `git add -A` in the main working copy sweeps in every worktree —
# an entire second checkout, committed by accident. Two things in `.claude/`
# belong to the repo: the overlay, and the project skills under `skills/`
# (added 2026-09-01 with `/frontier`). Everything else there is a worktree.
.claude/*
!.claude/end-session.md
!.claude/skills/

# Build artefacts from running the prototypes
*.beam
*.plt

# Gleam's own build cache, written by `gleam build`/`gleam deps download` under
# aoc/bench/gleam whenever a probe or benchmark run exercises it.
aoc/bench/gleam/build/

# A real fetched dependency (its own git checkout) used as scratch evidence
# for ticket 52's probes — not something to vendor as a nested repo.
artifacts/scratch/rebarlib/

# A crashed `erl` writes one of these wherever it was run. Committed once by
# accident (069fda7) and modified by a later session before being caught.
erl_crash.dump

# compiler build artefacts
compiler/_build/

# `rebar3` run from the WRONG DIRECTORY writes an empty `[].` lock file wherever
# it was invoked, and `git add -A` then commits it. It happened twice in one
# session — once at the repo root, once in the tree-sitter grammar directory —
# because a shell `cd` persists between commands and the mistake is silent:
# rebar3 succeeds, and the only trace is a four-byte file. The only real rebar
# project here is `compiler/`, so a lock file anywhere else is always this.
/rebar.lock
editor/**/rebar.lock

# `bsc` with no -o writes the serialised abstract format beside the source.
*.abstr
compiler/bench/*.beam
compiler/*.beam
compiler/src/bs_lexer.erl
compiler/src/bs_parser.erl
manifest.run.json

# `check-toolchain.sh` probes `erl` from a fresh directory it makes here, because
# the version manager resolves .tool-versions by walking up and a system temp dir
# has nothing above it. Removed on every path out of that function; this line is
# for the run that is killed between the mktemp and the rm.
.toolchain-probe.*

# Agent tooling writes `.agents/skills.json` and a tree of symlinks pointing at
# `.claude/skills`, which is already tracked. It is a generated index of a
# tracked directory, so committing it would be the same content under a second
# name — and an untracked one makes every `/frontier` run report a dirty tree.
.agents/
